  "basis": "reference-normalized medians over 2 run(s) (36414022857, 36334971340), each suite a multiple of the reference workload its own cell measured. Each suite is the mean of its measured head-round totals in that run, divided by its own cell's reference seconds; the warm-up round is discarded by the timed job's design and the base side is another tree, so neither is counted. target_cell_weight 25: the 328 recorded weights total 356.4 reference multiples and the 12 suites these runs did not measure add 2.542, 358.9 in all, which is 15 cells at that target; it is the smallest 5-unit step at which the planner's balance guarantee holds (heaviest cell 23.93 against a 23.93 median, margin 0.35) and the count fits the bound, so the target is measured rather than chosen. max_cells 15: the bound on the cells the planner derives; the measured run ran 5 cells, while this file derives 15 cells, so that run is not the matrix this file plans, and when the derived count reaches the bound the planner clamps and names the target the margin would need. 12 of the tree's 340 suites are not measured by these runs, 12 estimated at the median of the recorded weights: test_ci_wait_required.py, test_commit_step_seam.py, test_gitignore_control.py, test_launch_arm_cuts.py, test_launch_arms.py, test_planner_determinism.py, test_plant_restore.py, test_receiver_descent.py, test_timed_coverage.py, test_timed_coverage_bounds.py, test_timed_coverage_shapes.py, test_watcher_poll_index.py Re-derive with `python3 scripts/ci/refresh_timings.py --runs-root <downloaded runs> --out .github/suite-timings.json` (--seed for the first file from one run)."
